{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/design/yang.preludes.md | sed -n '226,452p'\"","aggregated_output":"   226\t- **`yrt.safepoint` (`pysp`, `jssp`):** Extracts `stream/cursor`, `stream/poll!` gap/signal detection, and `attach!` setup into a shared module (`yrt.safepoint`), leaving signal delivery policy (`KeyboardInterrupt` / registered signal handler in `pysp`; uncatchable root `Interrupt` unwind in `jssp`) and recursion depth counting (`pysp`) in each hook module.\n   227\t\n   228\t---\n   229\t\n   230\t## 5. Declarative prelude composition, recipes, and admission\n   231\t\n   232\tTo eliminate ad-hoc `module-spec` and `admit` boilerplate while keeping every runtime dependency completely reproducible and content-pinned, **build-time emission recipes** and **immutable deployment profiles** are separated cleanly.\n   233\t\n   234\t### 5.1 Emission recipe vs. resolved runtime profile\n   235\t\n   236\t1. **`:yang.prelude/recipe` (host-side compiler recipe that *emits* a runtime module):**\n   237\t   Used by `yang.core.prelude` + `yang.core.prelude-admission` to produce the module's UAST, schema-1 manifest, and C1 side table from the owning language's definition list.\n   238\t   ```clojure\n   239\t   {:yang.prelude/schema 1\n   240\t    :yang.prelude/id :yang.python/py-prelude\n   241\t    :yang.prelude/revision \"2026-11-20.1\"\n   242\t    :yang.prelude/module 'py\n   243\t    :yang.prelude/components\n   244\t    [[yang.call \"<blake3-address>\"]\n   245\t     [yrt.escape \"<blake3-address>\"]\n   246\t     [yrt.float \"<blake3-address>\"]\n   247\t     [yrt.int \"<blake3-address>\"]]\n   248\t    :yang.prelude/host-modules\n   249\t    {:cell {:required true}\n   250\t     :data {:required true, :min-max-items 1048576}\n   251\t     :integer {:required true, :min-bits 53}}\n   252\t    :yang.prelude/emitter\n   253\t    {:mode :linear                 ;; :linear (definitions->uast) | :balanced (balanced-definitions->uast)\n   254\t     :uninit :py/uninit\n   255\t     :rt-namespaces #{\"py.rt\" \"py.b\"}\n   256\t     :unshadow-locals? false\n   257\t     :finalize-c1? true            ;; annotate :yang/call-site per current module emitter\n   258\t     :capture-safe-primitives nil} ;; optional for bundled clj mode\n   259\t    :yang.prelude/max-effects nil  ;; optional effect-ceiling set; nil = derive without extra ceiling\n   260\t    :yang.prelude/refusal-ns \"yang.python.antlr\"}\n   261\t   ```\n   262\t2. **`:yang.prelude/profile` (immutable, content-addressed runtime profile after publication):**\n   263\t   Replaces the recipe's local build knobs with the **published content address of the owning runtime module itself** (`:yang.prelude/root-address`) alongside the pinned transitive closure:\n   264\t   ```clojure\n   265\t   {:yang.prelude/schema 1\n   266\t    :yang.prelude/id :yang.python/py-prelude\n   267\t    :yang.prelude/revision \"2026-11-20.1\"\n   268\t    :yang.prelude/module 'py\n   269\t    :yang.prelude/root-address \"<blake3-address-of-published-py-module>\"\n   270\t    :yang.prelude/components\n   271\t    [[yang.call \"<blake3-address>\"]\n   272\t     [yrt.escape \"<blake3-address>\"]\n   273\t     [yrt.float \"<blake3-address>\"]\n   274\t     [yrt.int \"<blake3-address>\"]]\n   275\t    :yang.prelude/host-modules\n   276\t    {:cell {:required true}\n   277\t     :data {:required true, :min-max-items 1048576}\n   278\t     :integer {:required true, :min-bits 53}}\n   279\t    :yang.prelude/max-effects #{}} ;; optional allowed-effect ceiling (nil if none beyond derived footprint)\n   280\t   ```\n   281\t   A `:yang.prelude/profile` contains zero host functions or closures and passes `yang.frontend/non-portable-path`. Its `:yang.prelude/root-address` ensures two profiles cannot claim identical identity while pointing at different owning prelude definitions.\n   282\t\n   283\t### 5.2 Composition rules and verified-closure admission\n   284\t\n   285\t`yang.core.prelude` and `yang.core.prelude-admission` enforce six fail-closed checks:\n   286\t\n   287\t1. **Verified artifact closure input (`validate-profile`):**\n   288\t   - Admission takes `(profile artifact-store registry)`, where `artifact-store` supplies an **immutable, verified map `{address -> verified-manifest}`** (never assuming a graph from bare `[sym addr]` pairs!).\n   289\t   - Checks that `:yang.prelude/root-address` and every address in `:yang.prelude/components` resolve in `artifact-store`, that the transitive `:requires` graph is finite and acyclic, and that the root module's manifest `:requires` exactly matches its declared component pins.\n   290\t2. **Export collision rule (qualified vs. projected):**\n   291\t   - Distinct Layer-2a/2b modules **may** share identical bare local export names (for instance, `yrt.float/abs` and `py/abs` coexist safely across qualified module borders).\n   292\t   - Collisions **are refused** whenever two components bind the same linker module symbol, when a local `module-definitions` key collides after namespace stripping, or when two source-facing `:ambient-projections` claim the same target identifier (`§6.3`).\n   293\t3. **Provenance-door security exclusion:**\n   294\t   - Validation verifies that no `yrt.*` manifest in the closure exports any `dsg__*` symbol or declares `:cell/new-provenance` or `:cell/provenance` in its derived effects.\n   295\t4. **Effect-ceiling verification (`:yang.prelude/max-effects`):**\n   296\t   - Rather than duplicating the manifest's derived effect set (honoring \"Derive, don't persist\"), `:yang.prelude/max-effects` is strictly optional. When present, admission checks `(clojure.set/subset? derived-transitive-effects max-effects)` and refuses if any transitive module or host declaration exceeds the ceiling.\n   297\t5. **Host-module and limit admission (`admit-profile`):**\n   298\t   - Verifies that `registry` supplies every required host export (`prelude-admission/admit`) and meets every numeric/data floor (`:min-bits`, `:min-digits`, `:min-max-items`) before any unit publishes or runs.\n   299\t6. **Dual-emitter preservation & Parity Law:**\n   300\t   - **Linked emission:** derives `:requires` and `:skip?` from `:yang.prelude/components`, emits `require` nodes in declared order, preserves `:rt-namespaces`, runs optional local unshadowing (`php`), and preserves exact C1 finalization (`:finalize-c1?` — matching `py`, `js`, `clj`, `yang.call` today while keeping `php` consistent).\n   301\t   - **Bundled emission (`compose-bundled`):** preserves existing ordering, `init!` placement, tail-marking, `:mode` (`:linear` vs `:balanced`, never silently altered because tree shape is content-addressed), and Clojure's custom preamble / `dsg__*` wrapper.\n   302\t   - **Bundled vs. Linked Parity Law:** Any program compiled under a composed prelude MUST produce identical outcomes in bundled and linked modes across the semantic, stack, and register VMs (and the AST walker once L-b lands).\n   303\t\n   304\t---\n   305\t\n   306\t## 6. Preludes as swappable libraries: the semantics descriptor contract\n   307\t\n   308\tMaking Layer-2a components reusable solves code duplication; making **Layer-2b/2c preludes swappable libraries** solves syntax-to-runtime coupling. A frontend like `yang.python` can then treat its runtime prelude as a pluggable library (`:yang.semantics/descriptor`).\n   309\t\n   310\t### 6.1 Level 1 vs. Level 2 library composition\n   311\t\n   312\t- **Level 1 — Ambient Library Projection:** Keep the frontend's native semantics (`py`, `js`, `php`) and link an external module (such as `clojure.core`) into its ambient lookup scope via `yang.call`.\n   313\t- **Level 2 — Pluggable Semantics Library:** Replace the frontend's lowering contract itself with a compatible prelude library (e.g., compiling Python syntax against `clojure.core` + `clj` directly onto persistent Yin data structures with zero value wrapping or marshalling).\n   314\t\n   315\tLevel 2 strictly subsumes Level 1: a semantics descriptor defines **both** what lowering emits for syntax constructs (`:yang.semantics/hooks` + `:yang.semantics/literals`) and which ambient modules/identifiers enter source scope (`:yang.semantics/ambient-modules` + `:yang.semantics/ambient-projections`).\n   316\t\n   317\t### 6.2 Core vs. Frontend ownership boundary\n   318\t\n   319\tTo preserve `yang.antlr.md` §3 (\"Yang core contains no enumeration of supported languages\"):\n   320\t- **`yang.core.semantics` (language-agnostic)** owns ONLY:\n   321\t  1. Generic schema validation for `:yang.semantics/descriptor`.\n   322\t  2. Pure, closed literal-strategy emission (`:raw`, `:float64-raw`, `:tagged-map`, `:raw-or-call`).\n   323\t  3. Generic capability lookup, hook-hygiene validation (every hook must be namespace-qualified), exact export verification against a verified artifact closure, and reserved-door projection checks.\n   324\t- **Each frontend package (e.g. `yang.python.antlr.contract`)** owns:\n   325\t  1. Its **fixed Hook ABI table** (`{hook-key {:arity n :required-by [...]}}`) specifying exact parameter conventions and structural lowering shapes for that frontend's grammar.\n   326\t  2. Structural AST lowering rules (e.g., how Python functions, loops, comprehensions, module packets, and `try`/`except`/`else`/`finally` marshal operands to those hooks).\n   327\t\n   328\t`yang.core.semantics` validates a descriptor **against the frontend-supplied contract table** — core never hardcodes Python, JS, or PHP syntax constructs.\n   329\t\n   330\t### 6.3 Portable `:yang.semantics/descriptor` schema\n   331\t\n   332\tA semantics descriptor contains **only portable data** (satisfies `yang.frontend/non-portable-path`):\n   333\t\n   334\t```clojure\n   335\t{:yang.semantics/schema 1\n   336\t :yang.semantics/id :yang.python/clojure-core-v1\n   337\t :yang.semantics/syntax :python\n   338\t :yang.semantics/prelude-module 'clj.py\n   339\t :yang.semantics/ambient-modules\n   340\t [{:module 'yang.call,     :address \"<blake3-address>\"}\n   341\t  {:module 'yrt.escape,    :address \"<blake3-address>\"}\n   342\t  {:module 'yrt.float,     :address \"<blake3-address>\"}\n   343\t  {:module 'yrt.int,       :address \"<blake3-address>\"}\n   344\t  {:module 'clj,           :address \"<blake3-address>\"}\n   345\t  {:module 'clojure.core,  :address \"<blake3-address>\"}\n   346\t  {:module 'clj.py,        :address \"<blake3-address>\"}]\n   347\t\n   348\t :yang.semantics/capabilities\n   349\t {:mutation/locals      :cell          ;; :cell | :single-assignment | :refused\n   350\t  :mutation/subscript   :refused       ;; :supported | :refused\n   351\t  :mutation/attribute   :refused\n   352\t  :mutation/delete      :refused\n   353\t  :scope/global         :supported     ;; per-module globals cell only\n   354\t  :scope/nonlocal       :supported     ;; lexical cells when :mutation/locals is :cell\n   355\t  :calls/positional     :supported\n   356\t  :calls/varargs        :supported     ;; *args\n   357\t  :calls/defaults       :refused\n   358\t  :calls/kwonly         :refused\n   359\t  :calls/kwstar         :refused\n   360\t  :calls/kwargs         :refused\n   361\t  :destructuring/unpack :refused       ;; explicit choice; or :supported via clj.py/unpack\n   362\t  :expr/comprehensions  :supported     ;; eager list/set/dict only; genexpr gated by :control/generators\n   363\t  :control/exceptions   :supported     ;; bare `except:` / `except as e:` + `finally` + `raise`\n   364\t  :control/except-typed :refused       ;; class-matched `except ExcType:` refused when :oo/classes :refused\n   365\t  :control/generators   :refused       ;; gates BOTH `yield`/`yield from` AND generator expressions\n   366\t  :control/with         :refused\n   367\t  :oo/classes           :refused\n   368\t  :modules/import       :ambient-only} ;; :supported | :ambient-only | :refused\n   369\t\n   370\t :yang.semantics/literals\n   371\t {:nil     {:kind :raw, :value nil}\n   372\t  :bool    {:kind :raw}\n   373\t  :str     {:kind :raw}\n   374\t  :float   {:kind :float64-raw}      ;; vs {:kind :tagged-map, :tag :py/float}\n   375\t  :int     {:kind :raw-or-call, :safe-max-bits 53, :overflow-op 'clj.py/int-lit}\n   376\t  :unbound {:kind :raw, :value :clj/unbound}}\n   377\t\n   378\t :yang.semantics/hooks\n   379\t {;; Arithmetic & comparisons — ALL namespace-qualified (hygienic, immune to guest shadowing)\n   380\t  :op/add           'clj.py/add\n   381\t  :op/sub           'clj.py/sub\n   382\t  :op/mul           'clj.py/mul\n   383\t  :op/truediv       'clj.py/truediv\n   384\t  :op/floordiv      'clj.py/floordiv\n   385\t  :op/mod           'clj.py/mod\n   386\t  :op/pow           'clj.py/pow\n   387\t  :op/neg           'clj.py/neg\n   388\t  :op/pos           'clj.py/pos\n   389\t  :op/eq            'clj.py/eq\n   390\t  :op/ne            'clj.py/ne\n   391\t  :op/lt            'clj.py/lt\n   392\t  :op/le            'clj.py/le\n   393\t  :op/gt            'clj.py/gt\n   394\t  :op/ge            'clj.py/ge\n   395\t  :op/lnot          'clj.py/lnot\n   396\t  :op/truthy        'clj.py/truthy\n   397\t  ;; Collections & indexing\n   398\t  :coll/vconj       'clj.py/vconj\n   399\t  :coll/list        'clj.py/list\n   400\t  :coll/tuple       'clj.py/tuple\n   401\t  :coll/set         'clj.py/set-from\n   402\t  :coll/dict        'clj.py/map-from\n   403\t  :coll/getitem     'clj.py/get-item\n   404\t  ;; Scopes & bindings\n   405\t  :env/local-get    'clj.py/local-get\n   406\t  :env/global-get   'clj.py/global-get\n   407\t  :env/global-set   'clj.py/global-set\n   408\t  ;; Functions & calls\n   409\t  :fn/arg           'clj.py/arg\n   410\t  :fn/make          'clj.py/make-fn\n   411\t  :fn/call          'clj.py/call\n   412\t  ;; Control flow & unit entry\n   413\t  :ctrl/for-each    'clj.py/for-each\n   414\t  :ctrl/try         'clj.py/try\n   415\t  :ctrl/try-finally 'clj.py/try-finally\n   416\t  :ctrl/raise       'clj.py/raise\n   417\t  :ctrl/call-ec     'clj.py/call-ec\n   418\t  :unit/run-main    'clj.py/run-main}\n   419\t\n   420\t :yang.semantics/ambient-projections\n   421\t {\"identity\"  {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'identity}\n   422\t  \"inc\"       {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'inc}\n   423\t  \"dec\"       {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'dec}\n   424\t  \"str\"       {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'str}\n   425\t  \"count\"     {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'count}\n   426\t  \"first\"     {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'first}\n   427\t  \"rest\"      {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'rest}\n   428\t  \"second\"    {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'second}\n   429\t  \"cons\"      {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'cons}\n   430\t  \"conj\"      {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'conj}\n   431\t  \"assoc\"     {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'assoc}\n   432\t  \"assoc_in\"  {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'assoc-in}\n   433\t  \"get\"       {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'get}\n   434\t  \"get_in\"    {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'get-in}\n   435\t  \"update\"    {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'update}\n   436\t  \"update_in\" {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'update-in}\n   437\t  \"map\"       {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'map}\n   438\t  \"filter\"    {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'filter}\n   439\t  \"reduce\"    {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'reduce}\n   440\t  \"into\"      {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'into}\n   441\t  \"keys\"      {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'keys}\n   442\t  \"vals\"      {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'vals}\n   443\t  \"merge\"     {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'merge}\n   444\t  \"is_empty\"  {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'empty?}\n   445\t  \"is_nil\"    {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'nil?}\n   446\t  \"is_map\"    {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'map?}\n   447\t  \"is_vector\" {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'vector?}\n   448\t  \"is_set\"    {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'set?}\n   449\t  \"ex_info\"   {:module 'clj.py,       :export 'ex-info}}}\n   450\t```\n   451\t\n   452\t### 6.4 Validation, lexical hygiene, authority checks, and address neutrality\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
