{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/design/yang.preludes.md | sed -n '453,677p'\"","aggregated_output":"   453\t\n   454\t1. **Hygienic generated references (no bare hook symbols):**\n   455\t   - Every symbol in `:yang.semantics/hooks` **MUST be namespace-qualified** (e.g., `clj.py/vconj`, `py/vconj`, `clj.py/add`). Unqualified symbols (such as bare `conj`, `+`, `not`, `set`) are rejected at validation (`:yang.semantics/unqualified-hook`), because bare symbols inside lowered UAST could be silently captured by a valid Python parameter or local named `conj` or `not`.\n   456\t2. **Scope-aware precedence for `:yang.semantics/ambient-projections`:**\n   457\t   - Free source identifiers resolve in strict order:\n   458\t     1. **Lexical scope** (`:local`, `:cell`, `:nonlocal` parameter or local variable, including a local named `map` or `conj`),\n   459\t     2. **Per-module globals** (`globals` dictionary via `:env/global-get`, allowing module-level `def` or `global` assignment to shadow an ambient binding cleanly),\n   460\t     3. **`:yang.semantics/ambient-projections`** (resolved via `clj.py/global-get` fallback to the module's explicit projected lookup map, or refused at runtime/admission if absent).\n   461\t   - Defining or binding a parameter named `conj` or `is_empty` shadows only that source lookup and **never** alters compiler-generated calls to `clj.py/vconj`, `clj.py/add`, etc.\n   462\t3. **Exact export & reserved-door authority validation (`validate-descriptor`):**\n   463\t   - Takes `(descriptor frontend-contract artifact-store registry)`:\n   464\t     - Verifies every hook required by `:yang.semantics/capabilities` is present, namespace-qualified, and exists as an **exact published export** in the corresponding manifest of `artifact-store` (or as a non-reserved export in a declared host module of `registry`, or an explicit non-reserved VM primitive in `yin.vm/primitives`). Namespace coverage alone is insufficient.\n   465\t     - Verifies every `:ambient-projections` target `{:module m :export e}` exists as an exact public export of `m` in `artifact-store` (and has unique source names).\n   466\t     - **Reserved-door ban:** Refuses any descriptor whose `:hooks` or `:ambient-projections` references `cell/dsg__*`, `dsg__*`, `yin/def`, `*.rt/*`, `*.b/*`, or `yang.safepoint/*`, or exposes any unprivileged raw primitive without projection. Registry availability never grants source-level authority.\n   467\t   - Any violation fails closed before reading CST packets with `:yang.semantics/invalid-descriptor`.\n   468\t4. **Fail-closed capability enforcement during lowering:**\n   469\t   - Before lowering any guarded CST construct (e.g., `classdef`, `yield_expr`, `genexpr`, `with_stmt`, `del_stmt`, typed `except E:`, keyword argument call, default parameter value, subscript assignment), the lowering checks the descriptor's capability map.\n   470\t   - Generator expressions MUST check `:control/generators` (so they cannot evade generator refusal even when `:expr/comprehensions` is `:supported`).\n   471\t   - Any disabled/absent capability emits:\n   472\t     ```clojure\n   473\t     {:status :refused\n   474\t      :reason :yang.semantics/unsupported-capability\n   475\t      :capability :oo/classes\n   476\t      :semantics-id :yang.python/clojure-core-v1\n   477\t      :construct \"classdef\"\n   478\t      :node <cst-node-id>}\n   479\t     ```\n   480\t5. **Byte-identical default-profile invariant (`P2`, zero golden churn for decoupling):**\n   481\t   - Refactoring `yang.python.antlr.lower` (in **Slice P2** — and subsequently TypeScript/PHP) to read from `:yang.semantics/descriptor` MUST emit **byte-identical UAST rows** under the default descriptor (`:yang.python/py-v1`, carrying all 103 `py/*` hooks, `{:kind :tagged-map, :tag :py/float}`, `{:kind :tagged-map, :tag :py/str}`, `:py/None`, and existing supported capabilities) compared to the pre-refactor hardcoded lowering. Zero existing golden addresses move in P2.\n   482\t\n   483\t### 6.5 Frontend SPI and provenance integration (`yang.frontend`)\n   484\t\n   485\tNo `yang.frontend` schema change is required (`src/cljc/yang/frontend.cljc`):\n   486\t- `:yang.frontend/id` continues to name the frontend syntax + lowering implementation (e.g., `:yang.python/antlr`), and each distinct configuration receives a distinct immutable `:yang.frontend/revision` (e.g., `\"py-v1\"` vs. `\"clojure-core-v1\"` — re-installing `[id revision]` with a different manifest returns `:yang.frontend/revision-conflict`).\n   487\t- `:yang.frontend/lowering-profile` pins the content address of the `:yang.semantics/descriptor` EDN artifact.\n   488\t- `:yang.frontend/runtime-profile` pins the content address of the resolved `:yang.prelude/profile` manifest.\n   489\t- Compilation provenance records `(cst-address, lowering-profile, runtime-profile, unit-address)` as data; note that distinct descriptors may legitimately yield identical UAST addresses on simple programs (many-to-one), so provenance retains the exact compilation tuple rather than inferring the descriptor from the UAST address alone.\n   490\t\n   491\t---\n   492\t\n   493\t## 7. Case study: `yang.python` with a `clojure.core` prelude (`:yang.python/clojure-core-v1`)\n   494\t\n   495\tThis section specifies the reference cross-paradigm profile in full, reconciling Python's lowering ABI, 4-host numeric portability, cross-unit callable admission, §8.10.7 exception bridging, and a portable `clojure.core` module.\n   496\t\n   497\t### 7.1 Value representation & semantic mapping\n   498\t\n   499\t| Python syntax | Native `py` prelude (`:yang.python/py-v1`) | `clojure.core` prelude (`:yang.python/clojure-core-v1`) |\n   500\t|---|---|---|\n   501\t| `None` | `:py/None` | `nil` |\n   502\t| `True` / `False` | `true` / `false` (numeric as `1`/`0`) | `true` / `false` (**non-numeric**: arithmetic raises guest error) |\n   503\t| `\"abc\"` | `{:py/str \"abc\"}` | `\"abc\"` (raw Yin/UTF-8 string) |\n   504\t| `42` | exact integer (safe raw, else `py/int-lit`) | exact integer (safe raw, else `clj.py/int-lit`) |\n   505\t| `1.5` | `{:py/float <float64>}` | `<float64>` (untagged Jing `data/float64` carrier) |\n   506\t| `[1, 2]` | cell `{:py/type :list :items [1 2]}` | persistent vector `[1 2]` |\n   507\t| `(1, 2)` | `{:py/type :tuple :items [1 2]}` | persistent vector `[1 2]` |\n   508\t| `{\"a\": 1}` | cell `{:py/type :dict ...}` | persistent map `{\"a\" 1}` |\n   509\t| `{1, 2}` | cell `{:py/type :set ...}` | persistent set `#{1 2}` |\n   510\t| `def f(x): ...` | cell `{:py/type :function :code (fn [args] ...) :yang.call/entry ...}` | authenticated cell `{:clj.py/type :function :name s :spec spec :yang.call/entry ...}` |\n   511\t| Truthiness | `0`, `\"\"`, `[]`, `{}`, `None`, `False` falsy | Clojure truthiness (`clj.py/truthy`): only `nil` and `false` falsy (`0`, `\"\"`, `[]` are truthy) |\n   512\t| Equality `==` / `!=` | `1 == 1.0 == True`, structural list/dict | Strict kind-preserving Clojure equality (`clj.py/eq`): `1 == 1` `true`, `1 == 1.0` `false`, `1 == True` `false`, `NaN == NaN` `false`, structural persistent `=` |\n   513\t\n   514\t*Truth-in-advertising invariant:* `:yang.python/clojure-core-v1` explicitly declares Clojure truthiness, persistent immutable collections, non-numeric booleans, and kind-strict equality as its support profile — never CPython parity.\n   515\t\n   516\t### 7.2 Portable numeric contract (`clj.py` over `yin.vm.integer` + `yrt.float` + `yrt.int`)\n   517\t\n   518\tPer `yang.antlr.md` §8.5.5, raw `+`, `-`, `*`, `/`, `<`, `<=`, `>`, `>=` on decoded `data/float64` carriers are **not portable across Node/JVM/Dart**. Therefore, `:yang.python/clojure-core-v1` routes ALL Python arithmetic, floor division, remainder, power, and comparison operators through `clj.py/*` adapters backed by `yin.vm.integer`, `yrt.float`, and `yrt.int` (requiring host `integer` module with `:min-bits 53`):\n   519\t\n   520\t1. **Kind classification (`clj.py/num-kind`):**\n   521\t   - `true`/`false`: non-numeric (raises guest error `{:clj.py/error :type-error ...}` on arithmetic/ordering).\n   522\t   - `(data/number? x)`: if `(data/content= x (data/float64 x))` then `:float`, else `:int` (this works uniformly on JVM, JS, Dart, and Jolt because `data/float64` carries its kind cleanly in `data/content=`).\n   523\t   - Anything else: non-numeric (except `+` / `*` if string concatenation/repetition is explicitly enabled or refused — in `v1`, `+` on strings concatenates via `data/str-concat` or refuses uniformly; `clj.py` documents exact string `+` support, keeping `*` numeric-only).\n   524\t2. **Int × Int:**\n   525\t   - `+`, `-`, `*`, `//`, `%`, `**` (`e >= 0`), comparisons: run through `integer/add`, `integer/sub`, `integer/mul`, `integer/floor-div-mod`, `integer/pow`, `integer/compare`, wrapping results with `yrt.int/check-limit` (translating `:yin.vm.integer/bit-limit`, `:digit-limit`, `:float-overflow` into catchable guest error maps via `clj.py/raise`). Check `divisor == 0` **before** calling `integer/floor-div-mod` or `integer/true-div` so caller defects never trigger operational host throws!\n   526\t   - `/`: checks non-zero divisor, calls `integer/true-div`, passes through `yrt.int/check-limit`, boxes result as `data/float64`.\n   527\t   - `**` with negative integer exponent: converts operands via `integer/to-float` (checked for `:float-overflow`) and delegates to `yrt.float/neg-pow`.\n   528\t3. **Float × Float and Mixed Int × Float:**\n   529\t   - Exact int operands promote via `(integer/to-float i)` (with `yrt.int/check-limit` handling `:float-overflow`).\n   530\t   - Carriers unwrap via `data/float-value` **only inside pure no-capture, no-safepoint leaf functions** in `clj.py` / `yrt.float`, compute `+`, `-`, `*`, `yrt.float/fdiv` (div-by-zero yields IEEE `±Inf`/`NaN`), `yrt.float/fmod-pos`, `yrt.float/fpow-half` / `yrt.float/neg-pow`, `yrt.float/floor-int`, and **immediately rebox** with `data/float64` before returning.\n   531\t   - Mixed ordering (`<`, `<=`, `>`, `>=`) rejects NaN (`false`) and delegates to `integer/compare-float` (without precision-losing float promotion!).\n   532\t4. **Equality (`clj.py/eq`, `clj.py/ne`):**\n   533\t   - Numbers use `data/content=` (so exact `1` ≠ float `1.0`, `0.0` vs `-0.0` follows `yrt.float/zero?` when comparing float zeros `(= 0.0 -0.0) -> true`, and `NaN == NaN` -> `false` explicitly); non-numbers use Yin `=` (`true` for equal persistent vectors/maps/sets/strings/nil/booleans).\n   534\t\n   535\t### 7.3 Python lowering Hook ABI & `clj.py` adapters\n   536\t\n   537\tRather than pretending `clj/*` shares identical signatures with `py/*`, the frontend keeps its fixed **Python Lowering Hook ABI** (`yang.python.antlr.contract`) and `clj.py` implements every hook with compatible arity and semantics:\n   538\t\n   539\t| Hook key | Frontend ABI signature | `clj.py` implementation |\n   540\t|---|---|---|\n   541\t| `:env/local-get` | `[cell name]` | Reads `(cell/get cell)`; raises guest unbound error if `:clj/unbound` (supporting parameter init, local reassignment, and `nonlocal` via shared lexical cells when `:mutation/locals :cell`). |\n   542\t| `:env/global-get` | `[globals-cell name]` | Reads the unit's **per-module** `globals-cell` first; on miss, falls back to `clj.py`'s explicit `:ambient-projections` lookup table; on miss there, raises guest `NameError`-equivalent map `{:clj.py/error :name-error :name name}`. Keeps distinct compiled modules isolated instead of sharing one flat `clj.rt/globals` map. |\n   543\t| `:env/global-set` | `[globals-cell name value]` | Writes `(cell/set! globals-cell (assoc (cell/get globals-cell) name value))` and returns `value`. |\n   544\t| `:fn/make` | `[fname spec defaults kwdefaults code]` | Accepts the exact 5 arguments from `yang.python.antlr.lower/function-value:1870` (lowering already refused defaults/kwonly/kwstar/kwargs when disabled); mints an **authenticated task-heap cell** (`§7.4`). |\n   545\t| `:fn/call` | `[callee args]` | Routes to `yang.call/invoke` with `clj.py`'s condition-unwrapping / provenance-retaining raise exit (`§7.4`), never bare `clj/raise`. |\n   546\t| `:ctrl/try` | `[body handler orelse]` | **3-arg signature** calling `yrt.escape/try-orelse` on `(clj/rt-ctx)`, preserving Python `try` / `except` / `else`. |\n   547\t| `:ctrl/try-finally` | `[body fin]` | Calls `yrt.escape/try-finally` on `(clj/rt-ctx)` with `normal-arg = nil`. |\n   548\t| `:ctrl/raise` | `[e]` | Calls `clj/raise` (delegating to `yrt.escape/raise` on `(clj/rt-ctx)`). |\n   549\t| `:ctrl/call-ec` | `[f]` | Calls `yrt.escape/call-ec` on `(clj/rt-ctx)` with `normal-arg = nil`. |\n   550\t| `:ctrl/for-each` | `[iterable step-fn]` | Iterates `(clojure.core/seq iterable)` via `first`/`rest`, invoking `step-fn` per element (supports `break`/`continue` via `call-ec` and eager comprehensions). |\n   551\t| `:unit/run-main` | `[body-fn]` | Calls `(clj/init!)` and `(clojure.core/init!)`; allocates a **fresh per-unit `globals` cell** (`(cell/new {})`) and `globals-fn`; invokes `(body-fn globals globals-fn)` inside a top-level handler; returns the value **verbatim without stripping `[:yin.k/ok ...]`** so ordinary Python data shaped like `[:yin.k/ok 42]` passes through uncorrupted. |\n   552\t\n   553\t*(Lowerings with `:mutation/locals :single-assignment` remain a separate, stricter profile variant that omits `cell/new`/`cell/set!` and refuses assignment/reassignment to locals, loops with mutated accumulators, and `nonlocal`.)*\n   554\t\n   555\t### 7.4 Cross-unit callable admission and §8.10.7 exception bridging\n   556\t\n   557\tAs established in `src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:1280–1306` and `2400–2424`, an immutable Clojure descriptor map requires a `:clj/admission` witness closing over that unit's private `dsg__call_token` — a map emitted by another module fails `yang.clojure`'s immutable-descriptor admission check. In contrast, **authenticated task-heap cells** (`cell/authentic?`, `clojure.cljc:2400–2408`) are admitted across **every** independently compiled unit (`yang.clojure`, `clojure.core`, `clj.py`, `py`, `js`, `php`).\n   558\t\n   559\tTherefore `clj.py` enforces the full §8.10 + §8.10.7 contract:\n   560\t\n   561\t1. **Trusted cell-backed callable constructor (`clj.py/make-fn`):**\n   562\t   - Allocates `(cell/new {:clj.py/type :function, :name fname, :spec spec, :yang.call/entry entry})`.\n   563\t   - Forged plain maps and forged `{:type :cell-ref ...}` shapes fail `cell/authentic?` inside both `yang.call/eligible?` and `yang.clojure`'s `dsg__admitted?`.\n   564\t2. **Entry boundary (inside `:yang.call/entry`):**\n   565\t   - Validates `invocation` (`yang.call/valid-invocation?`), refuses non-empty `:yang.call/named` (`:yang.call/unsupported-named`), and binds positional / optional `*args` parameters against `:spec` — transferring `:yang.call/arity` on mismatch **before entering the body** (binding-before-body protection).\n   566\t   - Executes `(body-fn args-vec)` inside `clj.py/try-orelse` (3-arg, `orelse = identity`). On escape with value `e`:\n   567\t     - Calls private `cell/dsg__provenance` on `e`: if non-nil (an authentic retained protocol condition from a deeper cross-language boundary), forwards that retained condition **directly** to `(get invocation :yang.call/raise)` without double-wrapping;\n   568\t     - Otherwise wraps `e` (including ordinary user maps that happen to carry `:yang.call/reason`!) via `(yang.call/thrown e)` and transfers it to `(get invocation :yang.call/raise)`.\n   569\t3. **Call-site boundary (`clj.py/call`):**\n   570\t   - Passes a dedicated `raise-exit` closure to `yang.call/invoke`:\n   571\t     - If `(= (get condition :yang.call/reason) :yang.call/thrown)`, calls `(clj/raise (get condition :yang.call/value))` (unwrapping user-thrown values identically to `clojure.cljc:1441–1447`).\n   572\t     - Otherwise retains the protocol condition inside a private provenance carrier `(clj/raise (cell/dsg__new-provenance condition condition))` (mirroring `clojure.cljc:1448–1450`), preserving full condition fidelity across A → B → A unwinds and `finally` blocks.\n   573\t   - `cell/dsg__new-provenance` and `cell/dsg__provenance` remain strictly private inside trusted Layer-2b `clj.py` (`module-uast` only), never exported or exposed to `yrt.*` or source scope.\n   574\t\n   575\t### 7.5 Portable `clojure.core` linked library contract\n   576\t\n   577\tIn Slice P3, `clojure.core` is published as an **explicit, standalone, portable linker module** (`clojure.core`) requiring `yang.call` and `clj`, and registered against host modules `kind` and `data` (strictly omitting host-dependent exports):\n   578\t\n   579\t1. **Portable subset extracted from `yang.clojure/library` (`src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:2603–2914`):**\n   580\t   - Exported definitions: `identity`, `inc`, `dec`, `second`, `not=`, `boolean?`, `fn?`, `update`, `count`, `contains?`, `symbol?`, `keyword?`, `int?`, `meta`, `name`, `symbol`, `keyword`, `str`, `fresh-symbol`, `gensym`, `last`, `butlast`, `nth`, `string?`, `with-meta`, `coll?`, `vector?`, `map?`, `set?`, `sequential?`, `seq?`, `list?`, `rest`, `seq`, `rem`, `reverse`, `cons`, `list`, `vector`, `reduced`, `reduced?`, `unreduced`, `reduce`, `map`, `mapv`, `filter`, `remove`, `into`, `concat`, `keys`, `vals`, `disj`, `union`, `difference`, `merge`, `comp`, `partial`.\n   581\t   - **Explicitly excluded for 4-host portability:** `var?` (CLJ-only in `kind-module:2593`) and `resolve` (`kind/resolve` absent from `kind-module`).\n   582\t2. **Newly authored portable helpers & primitive callable projections (not pre-existing in `yang.clojure/library`):**\n   583\t   - Pure guest additions in `clojure.core`: `assoc-in`, `update-in`, `get-in`, `hash-map`, `set`.\n   584\t   - **Primitive callable projections:** thin `yang.call`-admitted cell-backed callable wrappers over VM primitives (`nil?`, `empty?`, `not`, `first`, `conj`, `assoc`, `get`, `vec`) so Python source can either call `is_empty(xs)` directly OR pass `is_empty` as a higher-order callback to `filter`/`map`.\n   585\t3. **Per-task instantiation & sibling isolation:**\n   586\t   - Loading `clojure.core` defines pure lambdas only (zero task state at lift/link time). `(clojure.core/init!)` allocates the task's cell-backed `yang.call` descriptors once per task under internal `clojure.core.rt/*` cells (guarded by `clojure.core.rt/state`) and exports `(clojure.core/export sym)` for adapter lookup.\n   587\t   - Internal sibling calls inside `clojure.core` (e.g., `map` calling `seq`, `first`, `rest`, `cons`, `reverse`) bind directly to `clojure.core`'s own internal module definitions, never to guest globals, so a user `def map` or `def rest` in Python/Clojure cannot hijack library internals.\n   588\t4. **No implicit namespace dump & zero impact on default `yang.clojure` in P3:**\n   589\t   - Adding `'clojure.core` to `:requires` exposes nothing to user code on its own; only explicit entries in `:yang.semantics/ambient-projections` enter source scope.\n   590\t   - Existing `yang.clojure`'s `library-for` bundling stays untouched in P3 so default Clojure compilation keeps zero golden churn; migrating `yang.clojure` itself onto `clojure.core` is scheduled separately (owner decision D6).\n   591\t\n   592\t### 7.6 Concrete lowering example\n   593\t\n   594\t```python\n   595\tdef sum_even_squares(xs):\n   596\t    if is_empty(xs):\n   597\t        return 0\n   598\t    evens = filter(lambda n: n % 2 == 0, xs)\n   599\t    squares = map(lambda n: n * n, evens)\n   600\t    return reduce(lambda a, b: a + b, 0, squares)\n   601\t```\n   602\t\n   603\t- `is_empty` resolves (below lexical/module scope) via `:yang.semantics/ambient-projections` to `clojure.core`'s projected `empty?` cell-backed callable.\n   604\t- `filter`, `map`, `reduce` resolve to `clojure.core`'s task-instantiated cell-backed callables.\n   605\t- `%`, `*`, `+`, `==` lower hygienically to `clj.py/mod`, `clj.py/mul`, `clj.py/add`, `clj.py/eq` (exact `yin.vm.integer` / `yrt.float` paths).\n   606\t- `lambda n: ...` lowers to `clj.py/make-fn`, producing an authenticated cell-backed `yang.call` callable invoked directly by `clojure.core/filter` and `clojure.core/map`.\n   607\t- `sum_even_squares([1, 2, 3, 4])` evaluates `[1 2 3 4]` → `20` (exact persistent integer), and returns `20` unchanged (not unwrapped by `[:yin.k/ok ...]`).\n   608\t\n   609\t---\n   610\t\n   611\t## 8. Portability, content addressing, and malleability\n   612\t\n   613\t### 8.1 Multi-host portability (JVM, CLJS/Node, CLJD/Dart, Jolt/Scheme)\n   614\t\n   615\tAll new `yang.core.*` and `yang.rt.*` (`yrt.*`) namespaces live in `src/cljc/` and obey the repository's four-host constraints:\n   616\t- **ClojureDart AOT literal limits:** Consolidate `defquoted` (`yang.python.antlr.prelude`, `yang.typescript.antlr.prelude`, `yang.php.antlr.quoted`) into `yang.core.prelude/defquoted`, keeping identical `:cljs`/`:cljd` macro imports, reader aliases, and EDN expansion.\n   617\t- **No bare integral float literals & safe integer bounds:** `yrt.float` and `clj.py` construct every float constant via `data/float-value`/`data/float64`, `-0.0` via `(* (data/float-value -1) (data/float-value 0))`, and avoid integer literals past `2^53 - 1`.\n   618\t- **Canonical ordering (`b86bc0e8` invariant):** Recipes, profiles, descriptor maps, and emitted UAST operand sequences sort keys deterministically (`sort-by str` / explicit vector order) and never iterate host maps when building AST nodes, guaranteeing byte-identical `dao.jing.cbor` hashes across JVM, Node, Dart, and Jolt.\n   619\t- **No JVM-only reflection:** `yang.core.semantics` and `yang.core.prelude` use pure portable Clojure data transforms with zero `eval`, runtime `tools.reader`, or JVM reflection.\n   620\t\n   621\t### 8.2 Dependency graph and malleability (`docs/agents/malleability.md`)\n   622\t\n   623\tPreserves a strictly layered, cycle-free dependency graph verified with `clj ./bin/analyze-deps.clj`:\n   624\t\n   625\t```text\n   626\tLayer A (AST & Data Schemas):    yang.core.uast\n   627\tLayer B (Pure Composition):      yang.core.prelude, yang.core.semantics\n   628\tLayer C (Registry Admission):    yang.core.prelude-admission, yang.core.module, yang.core.publication\n   629\tLayer D (Shared Guest Modules):  yang.core.call, yang.rt.escape, yang.rt.float, yang.rt.int\n   630\tLayer E (Language Frontends):    yang.python.antlr.*, yang.typescript.antlr.*, yang.php.antlr.*, yang.clojure.*\n   631\t```\n   632\t\n   633\t- **Frontend isolation:** Frontend-specific hook ABI contracts (like `yang.python.antlr.contract`) remain in Layer E, never in `yang.core.*`.\n   634\t- **Bounded public APIs:** Host namespaces maintain 2–5 `defn` entry points (`yang.core.semantics`: `validate-descriptor`, `capability-status`, `literal-node`, `hook-symbol`, `resolve-ambient`), and guest `yrt.*` modules bound their public export count cleanly (grouping only cohesive primitives per module rather than creating a sprawling grab-bag).\n   635\t\n   636\t### 8.3 Content-addressing and golden migration discipline\n   637\t\n   638\t1. **Address-neutral slices (P0, P2, P3):** `P0` preserves exact pre-change UAST bytes on frozen snapshots; `P2` emits byte-identical UAST for every default language profile; `P3` adds `:yang.python/clojure-core-v1` and `clojure.core` without changing `yang.clojure`'s default `library-for` output or any existing language goldens.\n   639\t2. **One batched profile bump (`P1`):** Each `yrt.*` module (`yrt.escape`, `yrt.float`, `yrt.int`) is implemented and validated independently first, then activated across `py`, `js`, `php`, and `clj` in one coordinated profile bump so `:segment/blake3-*` goldens (`scanner_goldens.cljc`, `float_address_test.cljc`, `dht-import-v1.edn`, `clojure_callsite_test.cljc`, linked harnesses) refresh once.\n   640\t\n   641\t---\n   642\t\n   643\t## 9. Phased implementation roadmap and acceptance gates\n   644\t\n   645\t| Slice | Scope & deliverables | Golden impact | Concrete acceptance gate |\n   646\t|---|---|---|---|\n   647\t| **P0 — Composition plumbing & `defquoted` consolidation** | Consolidate `defquoted` into `yang.core.prelude`; implement `:yang.prelude/recipe` / `:yang.prelude/profile` composition and verified-closure validation in `yang.core.prelude` + `prelude-admission` (preserving operand sequencing, `init!` placement, tail marking, `:linear`/`:balanced` mode, and Clojure's custom preamble). | **Zero** (byte-identical emission) | Compare generated UAST/specs against frozen pre-change snapshots of `py`/`js`/`php`/`clj`/`yang.call`; test verified-closure edge validation, missing transitive artifact/export refusal, provenance-door/effect-ceiling exclusions, and projected-name collision refusal. |\n   648\t| **P1 — Layer 2a Tier 1 (`yrt.escape`, `yrt.float`, `yrt.int`)** | Implement the three stateless guest modules; migrate `js`/`clj` from 4-slot to 5-slot contexts (`:handlers :depth :base :frame`); preserve open non-`:finally` (`:generator`) boundary dispatch; add `dsg__add`/`dsg__lte` guest helpers for bundled `clj`; activate across `py`, `js`, `php`, `clj` in one coordinated bump. | **One batched bump** | Unit tests for `yrt.*` on semantic/stack/register VMs; existing Python & PHP generator tests green; 4→5-slot migration tests; PHP `abandon-to` / `call-terminal` & normal `finally` replacement (`:py/None`, `:js/undefined`, `:php/null`, `nil`); `1.1 ** 6` bit-pattern parity (`fpow-half` vs `fpow-base`); `yin.vm.integer` v4 three-reason translation without masking operational throws; no-capture float seams; independent concurrent `py`/`js`/`php`/`clj` tasks sharing `yrt.*`; bundled == linked + 4-host + CPython/Node/PHP oracle parity; `clj ./bin/analyze-deps.clj` clean. |\n   649\t| **P2 — Lowering parameterization (`yang.core.semantics` + frontend contracts)** | Implement generic `yang.core.semantics`; define `yang.python.antlr.contract` (then TS/PHP); refactor `yang.python.antlr.lower` to read literals/hooks/capabilities/projections from `:yang.semantics/descriptor` defaulting to `:yang.python/py-v1`. | **Zero** (byte-identical default output) | Byte-for-byte UAST equality test across the full corpus under `:yang.python/py-v1`; tests covering every supported lowering path and capability mode (`:cell`, `:single-assignment`, `:ambient-only`), unqualified-hook rejection, reserved-door projection ban, and explicit refusal of generator expressions when `:control/generators :refused`. |\n   650\t| **P3 — `clojure.core` prelude for `yang.python` (`:yang.python/clojure-core-v1`)** | Publish standalone portable `clojure.core` module (`§7.5`) + `clj.py` adapter + `:yang.python/clojure-core-v1` descriptor; leave `yang.clojure`'s default `library-for` untouched; wire `yang.frontend` multi-revision catalog selection. | **Zero** on existing languages | Cross-unit callable admission & forgery tests (plain maps, forged cell-refs rejected; `clj.py/make-fn` admitted by `yang.clojure` / `clojure.core` / `py` / `js` / `php`); lexical shadowing of projected names (`conj`, `is_empty`, `map`) leaving lowered UAST uncaptured; primitive callable projections (`filter(is_empty, ...)`); per-module `globals` isolation across two units; `[:yin.k/ok 42]` ordinary data returned unstripped; condition-shaped user throws vs. retained protocol exceptions (`A→B→A` `finally` cleanup); portable `clojure.core` subset excluding `var?`/`resolve`; 4-host execution parity. |\n   651\t| **P4 — Tier-2 shared modules (`yrt.gen`, `yrt.safepoint`)** | Extract parameterized `yrt.gen` (preserving Python `:base` rebasing vs. PHP direct context restoration and refcount cleanup) and `yrt.safepoint` (`stream/poll!` skeleton for `pysp`/`jssp`). | **One bump** (deferred) | Generator + safepoint parity suites across VMs/hosts, preserving PHP lifecycle/cleanup policy and non-rebasing context behavior vs. Python rebasing. |\n   652\t\n   653\t---\n   654\t\n   655\t## 10. Open owner decisions\n   656\t\n   657\t1. **D1 — Local mutation model for `:yang.python/clojure-core-v1`:**\n   658\t   - *Option A (Recommended — Architect concurred):* `:mutation/locals :cell` (task-heap cells holding pure persistent Clojure values, matching Python parameter binding, unbound reads, reassignment, loops, and `nonlocal` with per-module `globals` cells). Keep `:single-assignment` as a separate restricted profile.\n   659\t   - *Option B:* `:mutation/locals :single-assignment` only (refuses local reassignment).\n   660\t2. **D2 — Namespace prefix for Layer-2a shared modules:**\n   661\t   - *Option A (Recommended — Architect concurred):* `yrt.*` (`yrt.escape`, `yrt.float`, `yrt.int`, `yrt.gen`, `yrt.safepoint`) matching `yang.typescript.md` §17 and `yang.php.md` §9, implemented in Clojure under `src/cljc/yang/rt/*.cljc`.\n   662\t   - *Option B:* `yang.rt.*` for both Clojure namespaces and linker module names.\n   663\t3. **D3 — Python float tagging during P1:**\n   664\t   - *Option A (Recommended — Architect concurred):* Retain `{:py/float x}` behind a 2-line `py` boundary adapter around `yrt.float` so P1 stays a pure runtime extraction without shifting Python value semantics or equality.\n   665\t   - *Option B:* Migrate Python to untagged `data/float64` carriers in P1.\n   666\t4. **D4 — Batching P1 (`yrt.escape` + `yrt.float` + `yrt.int`) vs. per-module bumps:**\n   667\t   - *Option A (Recommended conditionally — Architect concurred):* Implement and test each `yrt.*` extraction independently first, then activate all three in one coordinated profile bump so `:segment/blake3-*` goldens refresh once.\n   668\t   - *Option B:* Ship each `yrt.*` module as a separate profile bump.\n   669\t5. **D5 — Cross-syntax identifier mapping for Clojure names (`?`, `!`, `-`):**\n   670\t   - *Option A (Recommended — Architect concurred):* Curated `:yang.semantics/ambient-projections` table validated against exact exports, lexical precedence, primitive callable projections, and reserved-door bans.\n   671\t   - *Option B:* Algorithmic mangling rule (`_q` / `_bang`).\n   672\t6. **D6 — Publishing `clojure.core` as a standalone linked module:**\n   673\t   - *Option A (Constrained, Recommended — Architect concurred):* Publish the portable `clojure.core` subset (`§7.5`) with per-task instantiation in P3 for `:yang.python/clojure-core-v1` and future profiles, while keeping `yang.clojure`'s default `library-for` bundling unchanged in P3 (migrating `yang.clojure` separately later so P3 moves zero Clojure goldens).\n   674\t   - *Option B:* Copy needed `library` definitions into `clj.py`.\n   675\t7. **D7 — Float exponentiation rounding (`py`/`js` half-power vs. `php` base squaring):**\n   676\t   - *Option A (Recommended for P1):* Export both `yrt.float/fpow-half` and `yrt.float/fpow-base` so P1 preserves bit-exact parity (`1.1 ** 6`: `0x1.c585058dde7acp+0` for `py`/`js` vs `0x1.c585058dde7abp+0` for `php`) across all existing oracles.\n   677\t   - *Option B:* Explicitly approve unifying PHP onto `fpow-half` (or `py`/`js` onto `fpow-base`) and update the affected language's oracle departure ledger.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
