(f a))\n  2900\t         ([x] (f a x))\n  2901\t         ([x y] (f a x y))\n  2902\t         ([x y z] (f a x y z))))\n  2903\t      ([f a b]\n  2904\t       (fn\n  2905\t         ([] (f a b))\n  2906\t         ([x] (f a b x))\n   510\t   ['subvec [2 3] data-subvec]\n   511\t   ['hash-set [0 :variadic] hash-set]\n   512\t   ['into [2] data-into]\n   513\t   ['str-concat [0 :variadic] str-concat]\n   514\t   ['str-length [1] str-length]\n   515\t   ['substring [2 3] substring]\n   516\t   ['str-index-of [2 3] str-index-of]\n   517\t   ['str-split [2] str-split]\n   518\t   ['str-join [2] str-join]\n   519\t   ['char-at [2] char-at]\n   520\t   ['str->code-points [1] str->code-points]\n   521\t   ['code-points->str [1] code-points->str]\n   522\t   ['str-compare [2] str-compare]\n   523\t   ['str-unit-length [1] str-unit-length]\n   524\t   ['str-unit-at [2] str-unit-at]\n   525\t   ['str-units [1] str-units]\n   526\t   ['units->str [1] units->str]\n   527\t   ['well-formed-utf16? [1] well-formed-utf16?]\n   528\t   ['number? [1] data-number?]\n   529\t   ['float64 [1] float64]\n   530\t   ['float-value [1] float-value]\n   531\t   ['content= [2] data-content=]\n   532\t   ['callable? [1] callable?]\n   533\t   ['map? [1] data-map?]\n   534\t   ['vector? [1] data-vector?]\n   535\t   ['string? [1] data-string?]])\n   536\t\n   283\t### 5.2 Composition rules and verified-closure admission\n   284\t\n   285\t`yang.core.prelude` and `yang.core.prelude-admission` enforce six fail-closed checks:\n   286\t\n   287\t1. **Verified artifact closure input (`validate-profile`):**\n   288\t   - Admission takes `(profile artifact-store registry)`, where `artifact-store` supplies an **immutable, verified map `{address -> verified-manifest}`** (never assuming a graph from bare `[sym addr]` pairs!).\n   289\t   - Checks that `:yang.prelude/root-address` and every address in `:yang.prelude/components` resolve in `artifact-store`, that the transitive `:requires` graph is finite and acyclic, and that the root module's manifest `:requires` exactly matches its declared component pins.\n   290\t2. **Export collision rule (qualified vs. projected):**\n   291\t   - Distinct Layer-2a/2b modules **may** share identical bare local export names (for instance, `yrt.float/abs` and `py/abs` coexist safely across qualified module borders).\n   292\t   - Collisions **are refused** whenever two components bind the same linker module symbol, when a local `module-definitions` key collides after namespace stripping, or when two source-facing `:ambient-projections` claim the same target identifier (`§6.3`).\n   293\t3. **Provenance-door security exclusion:**\n   294\t   - Validation verifies that no `yrt.*` manifest in the closure exports any `dsg__*` symbol or declares `:cell/new-provenance` or `:cell/provenance` in its derived effects.\n   295\t4. **Effect-ceiling verification (`:yang.prelude/max-effects`):**\n   296\t   - Rather than duplicating the manifest's derived effect set (honoring \"Derive, don't persist\"), `:yang.prelude/max-effects` is strictly optional. When present, admission checks `(clojure.set/subset? derived-transitive-effects max-effects)` and refuses if any transitive module or host declaration exceeds the ceiling.\n   297\t5. **Host-module and limit admission (`admit-profile`):**\n   298\t   - Verifies that `registry` supplies every required host export (`prelude-admission/admit`) and meets every numeric/data floor (`:min-bits`, `:min-digits`, `:min-max-items`) before any unit publishes or runs.\n   299\t6. **Dual-emitter preservation & Parity Law:**\n   300\t   - **Linked emission:** derives `:requires` and `:skip?` from `:yang.prelude/components`, emits `require` nodes in declared order, preserves `:rt-namespaces`, runs optional local unshadowing (`php`), and preserves exact C1 finalization (`:finalize-c1?` — matching `py`, `js`, `clj`, `yang.call` today while keeping `php` consistent).\n   301\t   - **Bundled emission (`compose-bundled`):** preserves existing ordering, `init!` placement, tail-marking, `:mode` (`:linear` vs `:balanced`, never silently altered because tree shape is content-addressed), and Clojure's custom preamble / `dsg__*` wrapper.\n   302\t   - **Bundled vs. Linked Parity Law:** Any program compiled under a composed prelude MUST produce identical outcomes in bundled and linked modes across the semantic, stack, and register VMs (and the AST walker once L-b lands).\n   303\t\n   304\t---\n   305\t\n   306\t## 6. Preludes as swappable libraries: the semantics descriptor contract\n   307\t\n   308\tMaking Layer-2a components reusable solves code duplication; making **Layer-2b/2c preludes swappable libraries** solves syntax-to-runtime coupling. A frontend like `yang.python` can then treat its runtime prelude as a pluggable library (`:yang.semantics/descriptor`).\n   309\t\n   310\t### 6.1 Level 1 vs. Level 2 library composition\n   311\t\n   312\t- **Level 1 — Ambient Library Projection:** Keep the frontend's native semantics (`py`, `js`, `php`) and link an external module (such as `clojure.core`) into its ambient lookup scope via `yang.call`.\n   313\t- **Level 2 — Pluggable Semantics Library:** Replace the frontend's lowering contract itself with a compatible prelude library (e.g., compiling Python syntax against `clojure.core` + `clj` directly onto persistent Yin data structures with zero value wrapping or marshalling).\n   314\t\n   315\tLevel 2 strictly subsumes Level 1: a semantics descriptor defines **both** what lowering emits for syntax constructs (`:yang.semantics/hooks` + `:yang.semantics/literals`) and which ambient modules/identifiers enter source scope (`:yang.semantics/ambient-modules` + `:yang.semantics/ambient-projections`).\n   316\t\n   317\t### 6.2 Core vs. Frontend ownership boundary\n   318\t\n   319\tTo preserve `yang.antlr.md` §3 (\"Yang core contains no enumeration of supported languages\"):\n   320\t- **`yang.core.semantics` (language-agnostic)** owns ONLY:\n   321\t  1. Generic schema validation for `:yang.semantics/descriptor`.\n   322\t  2. Pure, closed literal-strategy emission (`:raw`, `:float64-raw`, `:tagged-map`, `:raw-or-call`).\n   323\t  3. Generic capability lookup, hook-hygiene validation (every hook must be namespace-qualified), exact export verification against a verified artifact closure, and reserved-door projection checks.\n   324\t- **Each frontend package (e.g. `yang.python.antlr.contract`)** owns:\n   325\t  1. Its **fixed Hook ABI table** (`{hook-key {:arity n :required-by [...]}}`) specifying exact parameter conventions and structural lowering shapes for that frontend's grammar.\n   326\t  2. Structural AST lowering rules (e.g., how Python functions, loops, comprehensions, module packets, and `try`/`except`/`else`/`finally` marshal operands to those hooks).\n   327\t\n   328\t`yang.core.semantics` validates a descriptor **against the frontend-supplied contract table** — core never hardcodes Python, JS, or PHP syntax constructs.\n   329\t\n   330\t### 6.3 Portable `:yang.semantics/descriptor` schema\n   331\t\n   603\t- `is_empty` resolves (below lexical/module scope) via `:yang.semantics/ambient-projections` to `clojure.core`'s projected `empty?` cell-backed callable.\n   604\t- `filter`, `map`, `reduce` resolve to `clojure.core`'s task-instantiated cell-backed callables.\n   605\t- `%`, `*`, `+`, `==` lower hygienically to `clj.py/mod`, `clj.py/mul`, `clj.py/add`, `clj.py/eq` (exact `yin.vm.integer` / `yrt.float` paths).\n   606\t- `lambda n: ...` lowers to `clj.py/make-fn`, producing an authenticated cell-backed `yang.call` callable invoked directly by `clojure.core/filter` and `clojure.core/map`.\n   607\t- `sum_even_squares([1, 2, 3, 4])` evaluates `[1 2 3 4]` → `20` (exact persistent integer), and returns `20` unchanged (not unwrapped by `[:yin.k/ok ...]`).\n   608\t\n   609\t---\n   610\t\n   611\t## 8. Portability, content addressing, and malleability\n   612\t\n   613\t### 8.1 Multi-host portability (JVM, CLJS/Node, CLJD/Dart, Jolt/Scheme)\n   614\t\n   615\tAll new `yang.core.*` and `yang.rt.*` (`yrt.*`) namespaces live in `src/cljc/` and obey the repository's four-host constraints:\n   616\t- **ClojureDart AOT literal limits:** Consolidate `defquoted` (`yang.python.antlr.prelude`, `yang.typescript.antlr.prelude`, `yang.php.antlr.quoted`) into `yang.core.prelude/defquoted`, keeping identical `:cljs`/`:cljd` macro imports, reader aliases, and EDN expansion.\n   617\t- **No bare integral float literals & safe integer bounds:** `yrt.float` and `clj.py` construct every float constant via `data/float-value`/`data/float64`, `-0.0` via `(* (data/float-value -1) (data/float-value 0))`, and avoid integer literals past `2^53 - 1`.\n   618\t- **Canonical ordering (`b86bc0e8` invariant):** Recipes, profiles, descriptor maps, and emitted UAST operand sequences sort keys deterministically (`sort-by str` / explicit vector order) and never iterate host maps when building AST nodes, guaranteeing byte-identical `dao.jing.cbor` hashes across JVM, Node, Dart, and Jolt.\n   619\t- **No JVM-only reflection:** `yang.core.semantics` and `yang.core.prelude` use pure portable Clojure data transforms with zero `eval`, runtime `tools.reader`, or JVM reflection.\n   620\t\n   621\t### 8.2 Dependency graph and malleability (`docs/agents/malleability.md`)\n   622\t\n   623\tPreserves a strictly layered, cycle-free dependency graph verified with `clj ./bin/analyze-deps.clj`:\n   624\t\n   625\t```text\n   626\tLayer A (AST & Data Schemas):    yang.core.uast\n   627\tLayer B (Pure Composition):      yang.core.prelude, yang.core.semantics\n   628\tLayer C (Registry Admission):    yang.core.prelude-admission, yang.core.module, yang.core.publication\n   629\tLayer D (Shared Guest Modules):  yang.core.call, yang.rt.escape, yang.rt.float, yang.rt.int\n   630\tLayer E (Language Frontends):    yang.python.antlr.*, yang.typescript.antlr.*, yang.php.antlr.*, yang.clojure.*\n   631\t```\n   632\t\n   633\t- **Frontend isolation:** Frontend-specific hook ABI contracts (like `yang.python.antlr.contract`) remain in Layer E, never in `yang.core.*`.\n   634\t- **Bounded public APIs:** Host namespaces maintain 2–5 `defn` entry points (`yang.core.semantics`: `validate-descriptor`, `capability-status`, `literal-node`, `hook-symbol`, `resolve-ambient`), and guest `yrt.*` modules bound their public export count cleanly (grouping only cohesive primitives per module rather than creating a sprawling grab-bag).\n   635\t\ndocs/design/datom.world.md:26:- Do not introduce hidden global state.\ndocs/design/datom.world.md:32:- Do not lose information (unitarity): streams are append-only and no datom is destroyed, only reinterpreted. The Universal AST is never lost: it is always retrievable wherever code is lowered, by address or by a query over its datoms. Every derived form (semantic vector, native images, indexes) is an interpretation of it and may drop facts only because the AST remains.\ndocs/design/datom.world.md:104:consumer and duplicates authority over a fact a query derives fresh. The\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
