(compile-form % false env macro-env) operands)}\n  1603\t      tail? (assoc :tail? true))\n  1604\t\n  1605\t    ;; anything else: one guest invocation, in tail position when the call is\n  1606\t    :else\n  1607\t    (compile-guest-call (compile-form operator false env macro-env)\n  1608\t                        (compile-form (vec operands) false env macro-env)\n  1609\t                        env tail?)))\n  1610\t\n  1611\t\n  1612\t(defn compile-application\n  1613\t  \"Compile a function application to Universal AST.\n  1614\t\n  1615\t  Clojure: (+ 1 2)\n  1616\t  AST: {:type :application\n189:  [:yin.k/profile :yin.k/class :yin.k/arities :yin.k/effects\n210:      :effectful (if (seq (:yin.k/effects profile))\n212:                   :undeclared-effects)\n235:   or `:effectful` with a declared, non-empty `:yin.k/effects` set, with\n240:   identity-keyed `:callable-effects`, which the engine checks an\n253:      (update :callable-effects\n255:              (vm/callable-effects fns profiles))\n310:;; them through the module system, they return effects, and the engine\n385:;; interprets the effects they return. The heap is VM state, so a mutation\n394:  (make-effect :cell/new {:val v}))\n424:  (make-effect :cell/new-provenance {:val value, :provenance provenance}))\n449:  {'new (vm/primitive-profile 'new :effectful [1] #{:cell/new} :none)\n456:                                              #{:cell/new-provenance} :none)\n    52\t\n    53\tThis design is constrained directly by `docs/design/datom.world.md` and `src/cljc/yin/vm/docs/state.md`:\n    54\t\n    55\t### 2.1 Foundational axioms\n    56\t\n    57\t1. **Everything is a Stream:** Prelude selection, composition, and lowering are pure functions of explicit data configurations and CST streams. Any external effect a prelude needs (`stream/put!`, `stream/poll!`, host I/O) remains a declared Layer-4 effect in the module manifest; prelude composition adds no ambient I/O.\n    58\t2. **Interpretation Creates Semantics:** A CST packet carries syntax only; its runtime meaning emerges from the tuple `(cst-packet, lowering-profile, semantics-descriptor, runtime-profile)`. Interpreting one Python CST under `:yang.python/py-v1` (CPython semantics) versus `:yang.python/clojure-core-v1` (Clojure persistent-data semantics) is a direct realization of \"one truth, many perspectives.\"\n    59\t3. **Code and State are Datoms (and Unitarity / Derive-Don't-Persist):**\n    60\t   - Lowering preserves source CST identity; compiled UAST roots under different preludes have distinct content addresses (or identical addresses when two descriptors emit identical UAST) linked by explicit provenance datoms pinning `(cst-address, lowering-profile, semantics-descriptor, runtime-profile, unit-address)`.\n    61\t   - Zero new AST tags, zero VM opcodes, and zero manifest schema changes are introduced. Linker manifests retain schema 1, and C1 `:yang/call-site` tables continue to publish beside manifests rather than inside them.\n    62\t   - Composition facts (which `yrt.*` modules a prelude requires) live in the explicit module `:requires` DAG, never as a redundant tag in UAST rows.\n    63\t4. **Everything is a Continuation:** Shared control-flow primitives (`yrt.escape`) and coroutine stepping (`yrt.gen`) remain pure guest UAST over `%capture` and task-heap cells (`cell/*`).\n    64\t\n    65\t### 2.2 Non-negotiable invariants\n    66\t\n    67\t1. **No hidden global state — stateless `yrt.*` modules:**\n    68\t   - `yang.core.*` holds no mutable global registry of preludes or languages (`yang.frontend` immutable catalog rule).\n    69\t   - **Shared `yrt.*` modules own zero `*.rt/*` state cells.** Every stateful `yrt.*` function takes the caller's task-local state cell (e.g., `ctx-cell`) as an explicit parameter. When a single Yin task links `py`, `js`, `php`, and `clj` modules together via `yang.call`, each language maintains its own isolated handler stack and depth/base accounting inside its own `*.rt/ctx` cell rather than aliasing or corrupting another language's stack.\n    70\t2. **No implicit control flow:** All escapes remain explicit continuation invocations over an explicit handler chain.\n    71\t3. **No raw callbacks:** Policy hooks passed by a language prelude into `yrt.*` (`on-empty`, `on-range`, `on-underflow`, `on-bit-limit`, `on-digit-limit`, `on-float-overflow`, `fin`) are ordinary guest Yin closures, never host-boundary callbacks.\n    72\t4. **No shared mutable state:** Each language profile allocates its own task-local cells once per task in its own `init!` under its own private namespace (`py.rt/*`, `js.rt/*`, `php.rt/*`, `clj.rt/*`, `clj.py.rt/*`, `clojure.core.rt/*`).\n    73\t5. **No layer collapsing:** Parsing (host ANTLR boundary) → lowering (syntax + frontend lowering contract + semantics descriptor → UAST) → prelude composition & admission (pure spec/artifact verification; never publishes or executes) → publication/linking → VM execution stay separated across explicit stream/module boundaries.\n    74\t6. **No assumed graphs:** Every composed prelude declares an explicit, acyclic `:requires` DAG over an **immutable, verified artifact closure**. Missing exports, missing transitive artifacts, or cycles fail closed at validation/admission time before publication or execution.\n    75\t7. **No closed language registry (`yang.antlr.md` owner directive):** Neither `yrt.*` nor `yang.core.*` contains a `case`/dispatch over `:python`, `:typescript`, `:php`, or `:clojure`, inspects `:py/type`/`:js/type`/`:php/type`/`:clj/type` tags, or encodes language-specific lowering ABI tables.\n    76\t8. **Security boundary — VM provenance doors stay private:** Under `src/cljc/yin/vm/docs/state.md` and `src/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc`, `cell/dsg__new-provenance` and `cell/dsg__provenance` are reserved compiler/runtime-module doors whose names guest code must not forge or re-export.\n    77\t   - **`yrt.*` modules MUST NEVER wrap, mint, read, declare, or export provenance-door primitives or `:cell/new-provenance` / `:cell/provenance` effects.**\n    78\t   - **No descriptor hook or source-facing ambient projection** may expose `cell/dsg__*`, `dsg__*`, `yin/def`, `*.rt/*`, `*.b/*`, or `yang.safepoint/*` (`§6.3`).\n    79\t   - Retained protocol-condition provenance (`yang.antlr.md` §8.10.7) stays strictly inside each trusted Layer-2b runtime module's private exception boundary.\n    80\t\n    81\t---\n    82\t\n    83\t## 3. Three-layer prelude architecture\n    84\t\n    85\t`yang.antlr.md` §9.1 Layer 2 (\"Language intrinsics and preludes\") is decomposed into three explicit sub-layers, all expressed as ordinary Universal AST over existing host modules (`cell`, `data`, `integer`, `stream`, `kind`, `portable`):\n  3635\tstring or array as data leaves it unchanged; a foreign caller must not\n  3636\tguess its language or search an ambient namespace to invoke it. This is\n  3637\tsource resolution/projection, not a language-pair wrapper around an\n  3638\talready admitted function.\n  3639\t\n  3640\tCross-language passage must not allocate a replacement function cell.\n  3641\tReturned functions retain their original identity, captures, defaults,\n  3642\tbound receiver, properties, and static state. A receiving frontend's\n  3643\tcallable test follows this common eligibility rule rather than rejecting\n  3644\tforeign native tags. Foreign attribute access and type reflection remain\n  3645\tprofile-owned; callability grants no general right to interpret another\n  3646\truntime's cell layout.\n  3647\t\n  3648\tCompiler-internal lambdas and host functions do not acquire this\n  3649\tconvention merely by being applicable in Yin. A source import exposing\n  3650\tone must emit an entry from its declared signature and effect profile.\n  3651\tIt must not guess an opaque closure's signature or bypass host-effect\n  3652\tand custody rules. Internal helper calls need not construct records.\n  3653\t\n  3654\t#### 8.10.3 Invocation record\n  3655\t\n  3656\tThe invocation is an ephemeral in-machine value. These keys are proposed\n  3657\tvocabulary, not existing repository APIs:\n  3658\t\n  3659\t```clojure\n  3660\t{:yang.call/callee     f\n  3661\t :yang.call/positional [v0 v1 ...]\n  3662\t :yang.call/named      [[\"name\" value] ...]\n  3663\t :yang.call/raise      raise-exit\n  3664\t ;; Optional: presence means a receiver was supplied, even when nil.\n  3665\t :yang.call/receiver   receiver\n  3666\t ;; Optional: pinned argument-binding extension, for example locations.\n  3667\t :yang.call/binding-profile \"<content-address>\"}\n  3668\t```\n  3669\t\n  3670\tThe four required fields mean:\n  3671\t\n  3672\t- `:yang.call/callee`: the original resolved callable, including its\n  3673\t  identity. The invocation helper supplies it; an extracted entry must\n  3674\t  not be applied to another object's substituted state.\n  3675\t- `:yang.call/positional`: a dense ordered vector of evaluated values.\n  3676\t  Its length records presence; no missing-argument sentinel is inserted.\n  3677\t- `:yang.call/named`: ordered name/value pairs, not a map. Names are\n  3678\t  plain text without caller-side case folding or normalization.\n  3679\t  Duplicate names remain visible until the callee's binder decides them.\n  3680\t- `:yang.call/raise`: this activation's caller-supplied, non-returning\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_23","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'dsg__|provenance|trusted' src/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc | tail -40\nnl -ba docs/design/yang.antlr.md | sed -n '3590,3635p'\nrg -n 'get hs|dsg__get' src/cljc/yang/clojure/prelude.cljc | head -16\nrg -n 'cell|task-local|module' docs/agents/malleability.md | head -15\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_23","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'dsg__|provenance|trusted' src/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc | tail -40\nnl -ba docs/design/yang.antlr.md | sed -n '3590,3635p'\nrg -n 'get hs|dsg__get' src/cljc/yang/clojure/prelude.cljc | head -16\nrg -n 'cell|task-local|module' docs/agents/malleability.md | head -15\"","aggregated_output":"180:;; A host module is the trusted composition boundary (yin.vm.linker.md\n184:;; publishes with it and answers for as trusted, reviewed code.\n292:;; the trusted constructor for host code; it is never a guest primitive or\n417:(defn new-provenance-cell\n419:   `provenance` installed in its private `:provenance` sibling, atomically.\n420:   `provenance` must be non-nil and is otherwise opaque to the VM. Only the\n421:   mint attaches provenance, and only at allocation. Not a guest surface:\n422:   the name is compiler-private (`dsg__`).\"\n423:  [value provenance]\n424:  (make-effect :cell/new-provenance {:val value, :provenance provenance}))\n427:(defn provenance-cell\n428:  \"The private reader: the `:provenance` a live, authenticated, marked cell\n432:   the name is compiler-private (`dsg__`).\"\n434:  (make-effect :cell/provenance {:cell candidate}))\n439:   two `dsg__` bindings are the compiler-private provenance mint and reader:\n442:   'dsg__new-provenance new-provenance-cell,\n443:   'dsg__provenance provenance-cell})\n454:   'dsg__new-provenance (vm/primitive-profile 'dsg__new-provenance\n456:                                              #{:cell/new-provenance} :none)\n457:   'dsg__provenance (vm/primitive-profile 'dsg__provenance\n459:                                          #{:cell/provenance} :none)})\n  3590\tby the callable constructors or import/export projections of a pinned,\n  3591\tconforming profile. The entry slot is a runtime descriptor field, not a\n  3592\tsource property that promotes arbitrary data to a function. A Python\n  3593\tdictionary, JavaScript object, or PHP array containing a source key\n  3594\tspelled `:yang.call/entry` remains ordinary source data unless an explicit\n  3595\tprofile-defined projection makes it a callable descriptor. Source\n  3596\tproperty access must not overwrite or masquerade as this runtime slot.\n  3597\tThis is an obligation of construction and source resolution, not a new\n  3598\tVM type, descriptor seal, or runtime provenance/language registry. Once\n  3599\tthe resolved descriptor is admitted, the shared projection is structural;\n  3600\tUAST deliberately constructing a conforming descriptor opts into the\n  3601\tconvention rather than changing a source language's data-map semantics.\n  3602\t\n  3603\tMissing entry means not callable. Constructors must install a genuine\n  3604\tunary Yin closure, and supported source mutations must preserve that\n  3605\tinvariant. Unary arity is a constructor/profile conformance obligation,\n  3606\tnot a signature introspection operation: Yin closures are opaque and the\n  3607\tVM's existing argument binding does not enforce this convention's arity.\n  3608\tA key in a map grants no VM privilege; application, ownership, and\n  3609\teffect checks still apply. A non-applicable entry remains an operational\n  3610\tVM application defect, not a source exception caught by the shared helper.\n  3611\t\n  3612\tFor callable kinds whose eligibility can change, the same cell or\n  3613\tdescriptor may also contain `:yang.call/eligible?`, a unary Yin predicate\n  3614\ton the original callable. Without it, an entry is eligible by default.\n  3615\tWith it, the common callable test uses its boolean result. The predicate\n  3616\treads explicit runtime metadata/heap only; it must not mutate state,\n  3617\tevaluate arguments, execute the target body, or invoke getters/user hooks.\n  3618\tIt has the same constructor/arity obligations as the entry. For example,\n  3619\tan instance can keep one dispatch entry while eligibility follows whether\n  3620\tits class currently supplies a supported call method; changing the class\n  3621\tdoes not require rewriting every instance.\n  3622\t\n  3623\tCall eligibility is tested at the callability-check point required by\n  3624\tthe caller's source, not universally before argument evaluation. The\n  3625\tentry resolves/rechecks a dynamic target at its source-required dispatch\n  3626\tpoint so argument side effects that change eligibility remain visible.\n  3627\tStatic callable kinds need no predicate.\n  3628\t\n  3629\tSource callable designators, such as PHP function-name strings and\n  3630\tcallable arrays where supported, are resolved under their source's rules\n  3631\tbefore common invocation. They do not gain entry slots merely by being\n  3632\tstrings or arrays. Exporting a designator as a first-class callable needs\n  3633\tan explicit frontend projection to an admitted descriptor, retaining any\n  3634\tsource-required late lookup and receiver semantics. Passing the raw\n  3635\tstring or array as data leaves it unchanged; a foreign caller must not\n112:    [clj/frame-depth (fn [hs] (if (nil? hs) 0 (get hs 3)))]\n119:       (cell/set! clj.rt/ctx (assoc (cell/get clj.rt/ctx) :handlers (get hs 2))))]\n129:           (if (= (get hs 0) :finally)\n130:             (do (clj/pop-frame hs) ((get hs 1) e) (clj/raise e))\n131:             ((get hs 1) e)))))]\n38:  - High `in` is good for foundational modules (like `dao.stream`, `yin.vm`)\n39:  - High `in` means this module is central/widely used\n46:- **Architectural Coupling**: High `out` to *highly stable foundational modules* (e.g., `dao.stream`, `yin.vm`). If the dependencies are bedrock primitives that change rarely, the coupling is stable and necessary for a layered architecture (e.g., the VMs).\n47:- **Accidental Coupling**: High `out` to *volatile leaf modules* or *unrelated feature sets*. This is a red flag indicating a lack of cohesion and is the primary target for refactoring.\n51:- High `out` for a leaf module = too many dependencies, extract shared concerns\n60:- **Layered graph** (good): Clean separation between modules, minimal cross-connections, clear flow from low-level primitives to high-level features. Layers are visually distinct.\n70:Bounded complexity is a natural consequence of clustering: when you extract dependent code into a namespace and expose only what's necessary at the boundary, you've created a module with bounded complexity.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
